  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Caprylic acid may interact with Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase through a series of target relationships. Specifically, Caprylic acid is associated with the cell line T-24, which is a target of multiple compounds, including Carvyl acetate and Phlegmanol C. These compounds, in turn, are targets of Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. This indicates that Caprylic acid may exert its biological effects through a pathway that involves T-24 and ultimately Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. The scores for these relationships are consistent, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Caprylic acid influences the activity of Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. The evidence is supported by multiple independent pathways, reinforcing the likelihood of a functional relationship between Caprylic acid and this enzyme.",
